# Vite loads this automatically for `vite build` (production mode), overriding .env for
# the same keys — see https://vitejs.dev/guide/env-and-mode. A real process/shell env var
# still wins over this file (e.g. the Dockerfile's `ENV VITE_API_BASE=...`), so this only
# takes effect for a plain `npm run build` with no VITE_API_BASE already exported — which
# is how the live site at https://devops.evyoog.com actually gets built and synced to its
# S3 bucket: it's static hosting behind CloudFront with no server-side layer to reverse-
# proxy `/api/*` the way nginx.conf does for a Docker deployment, so the relative
# VITE_API_BASE=/api/v1 in .env resolved to devops.evyoog.com itself — which has no /api
# route at all, so CloudFront's SPA-fallback served index.html back as the "response" to
# every login attempt. Pointing this build straight at the real backend sidesteps needing
# any reverse proxy at all; see SecurityConfig.java's vyoog.cors-allowed-origins for the
# matching backend-side change that allows https://devops.evyoog.com to call it directly.
VITE_API_BASE=https://req-api.evyoog.com/api/v1
